# Zero the LIO odometry and carry the robot's map pose across the jump -- the
# legged-robot counterpart of resetting a wheel encoder. Served by
# localizer_node (the workspace's syncai_localizer) on the relative name
# `reset_odometry`, in the bare robot_id namespace, so it lands on
# <robot_id>/reset_odometry, next to relocalize / auto_localize. New in
# 2026-10; the backend calls it with skip_seed behind
# POST /api/v1/localization/auto (kidnap recovery), with a 40 s client timeout.
#
# WHY IT IS NOT JUST pointlio/reset. ResetLIO restarts Point-LIO with its odom
# origin wherever the robot stands, but the localizer's map -> pointlio_odom
# correction was solved against the OLD origin: after a bare ResetLIO the
# localizer's next ICP guess is that old correction applied to an identity
# odom pose, which has nothing to do with where the robot is, and it never
# converges. AutoLocalize does not rescue it either while its scan window still
# holds scans posed by the diverged solution. This service does the whole
# sequence in one place: it calls pointlio/reset, drops every scan and odom
# sample of the old run (the ResetLIO.last_odom_time gate), seeds the map pose
# of the new run, and waits for the localizer's own registration to confirm it.
#
# The seed, in order of preference:
#   1. use_hint: x / y / yaw below (map frame) -- an operator's click on the
#      gridmap. z, roll and pitch are never taken from the request: z comes from
#      the last trusted registration, roll / pitch from the new run's own
#      gravity alignment (a flat guess never converges on the tilted mount; see
#      Relocalize's note on initialpose).
#   2. otherwise the localizer's last TRUSTED registration: the last ICP result
#      that converged while the odometry it was chained to moved at a plausible
#      speed. A diverged Point-LIO can still drag one ICP round to "converged";
#      the speed gate is what keeps that one out of the seed. If the robot
#      moved after that registration (it usually did -- divergence tends to
#      start with motion), the seed is off by that much, and step 3 is the net.
#   3. global_fallback: when the seed does not converge, run AutoLocalize's
#      hint-free search over the map's poses.txt keyframes, on scans of the new
#      run only.
# skip_seed bypasses all three: no seed is tried, and the global search runs
# as soon as the new run has filled the search's scan window. That is the
# kidnap case -- the robot was carried, so the last trusted registration is
# wrong by definition (and, right after boot, there is none), and trying it
# first costs converge_timeout_sec and risks converging on a look-alike spot.
#
# THE ROBOT MUST BE STANDING STILL, for the whole call. Point-LIO re-runs its
# static, gravity-aligning IMU initialisation (see ResetLIO); one done in
# motion tilts the new odometry for the rest of the run, with no error
# anywhere. Nothing here can enforce it; stop the robot (cancel navigation)
# before calling.
#
# SUCCESS IS A RESULT, NOT A RECEIPT, like AutoLocalize. The call blocks for at
# most the sum of the node's reset_odom.lio_reset_timeout_sec +
# reset_odom.wait_lio_timeout_sec + reset_odom.converge_timeout_sec, plus
# AutoLocalize's two deadlines when global_fallback is taken (2 + 10 + 5, + 15
# s by default) -- a client timeout must exceed that. With skip_seed it is
# lio_reset_timeout_sec + wait_lio_timeout_sec (which also bounds the wait for
# the scan window) + AutoLocalize's two deadlines (2 + 10 + 10 + 5 = 27 s by
# default), with no seeded wait in between. On failure the odometry
# has still been reset (that step is not undone) and the map -> pointlio_odom
# correction is left at the seed, so TF stays continuous; retry with a hint, or
# publish initialpose.

# Use x / y / yaw as the seed instead of the last trusted registration.
bool use_hint
# Map frame, metres / radians. Read only when use_hint is true.
float32 x
float32 y
float32 yaw
# When the seed does not converge, try the hint-free global search before
# giving up.
bool global_fallback
# Try no seed: reset, then go straight to the hint-free global search on
# new-run scans. use_hint and global_fallback are ignored when set. Needs a
# map saved with save_patches (poses.txt), like AutoLocalize.
bool skip_seed
---
bool success
# What happened at each step, or why it stopped.
string message
# Which seed the reported pose came from: "hint", "last_good" or "global".
# Empty when the call stopped before seeding (no seed, or the LIO reset
# itself failed), and with skip_seed until the search has found a pose.
string method
# The seeded (on failure) or converged (on success) map pose of the robot.
# Angles in radians.
float32 x
float32 y
float32 yaw
# The global search's measurements, as in AutoLocalize.Response. Filled only
# when method is "global" (the search found a pose, converged or not); zero
# otherwise.
float32 z
float32 fitness
float32 inlier_ratio
int32 candidates
